{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swami\/origamimappings"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Swami"}],"title":"Origami → SwiftUI mappings","roleHeading":"Article"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How Swami translates the four kinds of Origami patch into SwiftUI’s state graph."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Reference","anchor":"Reference","identifiers":["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Beats"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Origami’s patch graph and SwiftUI are both reactive dataflow, so the translator","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"targets SwiftUI’s ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"state graph","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" — computed properties, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"text":" —","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not imperative functions. Each row below is a rule the codegen applies; the helper","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"library ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Drag"},{"type":"text","text":", …) fills the gaps where a patch has no direct"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI equivalent."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"The four rules","level":2,"anchor":"The-four-rules","type":"heading"},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pure value patch (Add, Transition\/interpolate, logic)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"computed property \/ expression","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Interaction (Tap, Down\/press, Double Tap, Long Press)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"gesture + "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@GestureState"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"origami.drag"},{"type":"text","text":" — Drag"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"drag(enable:momentum:bounds:position:translation:velocity:reset:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (helper)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"State\/memory (Switch, Sample and Hold)","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" + update logic","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Animation (Classic Animation, Pop\/Spring)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".animation(.spring)"}]}]]],"header":"row","type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Origami layer tree becomes the SwiftUI "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View"},{"type":"text","text":" body. Origami "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Transition"},{"type":"text","text":" means"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"interpolation (not SwiftUI’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".transition()"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier — that’s a different concept)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Pure value patch → computed property","level":3,"anchor":"Pure-value-patch-%E2%86%92-computed-property","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Add","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Transition\/interpolate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and other pure-function patches carry no state.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"They fan an input through math and emit an output. In SwiftUI that’s a computed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"property (or an inline expression) — no ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", no side effect.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Interaction → gesture + `@State`","level":3,"anchor":"Interaction-%E2%86%92-gesture-+-State","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Origami’s Interaction patch exposes discrete output ports: ","type":"text"},{"code":"down","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"position","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"onTap","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"onDoubleTap","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"onLongPress","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Each maps to a SwiftUI gesture recognizer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whose output lands in ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or fires a callback. The ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" helper","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attaches only the recognizer for each output the caller requests, which keeps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"gesture arbitration clean.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"State\/memory → `@State` + update logic","level":3,"anchor":"Statememory-%E2%86%92-State-+-update-logic","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Switch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sample and Hold","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" remember a value across evaluations. That’s what","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is for. Codegen emits the state variable plus the update path (a gesture","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"callback, a ","type":"text"},{"code":".onChange","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or an assignment inside a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"text":" block).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Animation → `withAnimation` \/ `.animation`","anchor":"Animation-%E2%86%92-withAnimation--animation"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Classic Animation"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Pop Animation"},{"text":", and other animation patches drive a value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"toward a target over time. In SwiftUI, that’s a state change wrapped in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"text":" or an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".animation(_:value:)"},{"text":" modifier on the animated property.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Continuous-time springs that don’t have a stock SwiftUI equivalent get flagged","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by the parser — Swami won’t fake them.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Flag, don’t fake","anchor":"Flag-dont-fake"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Some Origami semantics don’t have a SwiftUI equivalent. When the parser hits one,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it emits a marker in the IR and codegen surfaces the gap rather than papering over","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it. The current list: continuous-time springs, custom JavaScript patches,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"absolute-position layout.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":